    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d285">

                <pb facs="0409" n="329" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg329"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            Squiers</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-07-15"><hi rendition="#italic">July 15,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 43.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In reply to your No. 60 of the 7th instant,
                    I have to say that you may convey to the Cuban Government an appropriate
                    expression of this Government’s appreciation of the action of the Cuban house of
                    representatives in adjourning in honor of the Fourth of July.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
